==Background==
ONEOK Partners LP’s Midwestern Gas Transmission Pipeline is a natural gas pipeline. It's 366 miles, but with connections to larger systems and the ability to move gas bidirectionally from Chicago and the Ohio River Valley. The system has a total capacity of 650 million cubic feet per day and seven compressor stations. The pipeline is connected to Alliance Pipeline, Northern Border Pipeline, Tennessee Gas Pipeline, Trunkline and Texas Gas Transmission. <ref name = source1> [https://www.midstreambusiness.com/midwestern-gas-transmission-smaller-size-important-value-209866 "Midwestern Gas Transmission: Smaller In Size, But Important In Value"] Midstream Business accessed January 2018 </ref> It extends from Portland, Tennessee to Joliet, Illinois. <ref name = source2> [https://www.bloomberg.com/research/stocks/private/snapshot.asp?privcapId=794025 "Company Overview of Midwestern Gas Transmission Company"] Bloomberg accessed January 2018 </ref> The gas is supplied from both Canada via the Alliance Gas Pipeline and domestically from the Rockies Express Gas Pipeline. <ref name = source3> [http://abarrelfull.wikidot.com/midwestern-gas-transmission-company-gas-pipeline "Midwestern Gas Transmission Company Gas Pipeline"] A Barrel Full accessed January 2018 </ref>

